Subject: [PATCH 6/9] The fixes' claims each have a test that fails without
 them, a real agent's panel and an earlier agreement included

Mutation-testing the review's fixes left one claim unheld: a voice contract's clause read from the first agreement on
the record passed, since every life had only the one in force. The offer twins now carry an earlier agreement that ended
a month before, so a clause that reads anything but the agreement the work is made under (owedAgreement) says the wrong
thing. Two more claims had no test at all: the Terms panel's line that a real agent's answer is the game's (a real
agent's offer, drawn), and the guide's example and end of term (pinned to TERMS and the factors its setup names).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
